      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Named after pioneer farmer Cooper, who built the first wood‑frame house in the area in 1880, the town carries his legacy.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cooperstown%2C_North_Dakota",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Cooperstown proudly serves as the county seat of Griggs County, a title it secured after a spirited battle over county records.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        8,
        9,
        10,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cooperstown%2C_North_Dakota",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Griggs County Courthouse, completed in 1884, stands as a historic reminder of the town’s early civic life.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cooperstown%2C_North_Dakota",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Cooperstown experiences a humid continental climate, with cold, snowy winters and warm, wetter summers that shape local life.",
